  "body": "My reading of #process-a-navigate-fetch is that the variable |reservedEnvironment| and request's reserved client can be coalesced, and I think having them be separate is confusing (took me a while to make sure nothing relied on them being different variables and I'm pretty sure I'm right). I believe they can be coalesced because:\n- We unconditionally set request's reserved client to |reservedEnvironment| on each iteration of the while loop\n- Whenever we make changes to |reservedEnvironment|, we only do so before we do what I mention above\n- There is one usage of |reservedEnvironment| after we set request's reserved client to it, but it is not mutated by its user, and we can just use request's reserved client in that case\n\nIf this change is not inadvertently breaking things, which I don't think it does, then I think this is a positive, simplifying change. But if others disagree I can reconsider.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/6471/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Last updated on Mar 10, 2021, 9:04 AM UTC (5b4a4a1)\">/browsing-the-web.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/6471/5161e49...5b4a4a1/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Last updated on Mar 10, 2021, 9:04 AM UTC (5b4a4a1)\">diff</a> )",
